    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Hydrocortisone cream, when needed.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:48",
      "end_timestamp": "00:50",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "So, um, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:53",
      "end_timestamp": "01:03",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Do you remember what it's for?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:05",
      "end_timestamp": "01:07",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Let me think, for my cholesterol, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I take furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning. Oh, I take moisturiser, several times a day. Oh, I was on lansoprazole before. I stopped taking it.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:08",
      "end_timestamp": "01:36",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]",
        "medications[2]",
        "medications[3]",
        "medications[4]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "How long has it been like this?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:37",
      "end_timestamp": "01:40",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Let me think, I'd say two weeks, maybe.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:42",
      "end_timestamp": "01:46",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "caregiver",
      "transcript_text": "I, I think it's been nearer three weeks, actually.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:48",
      "end_timestamp": "01:52",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:54",
      "end_timestamp": "01:58",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I, I suppose so, yes.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:59",
      "end_timestamp": "02:02",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps.",
